{"id":"refine_20260929114448714","summary":"Saved a cautious global memory for ARC tasks where aligned marker cells may be connected through the background.","rationale":"The solved instance had a uniform background 7 and marker cells 8 in one column; the two cells between consecutive markers were changed to 3 while the markers and other cells remained unchanged. The demonstrations also showed interval-filling behavior, but the rule should be applied only when supported by the task examples.","expectedOutcome":"For similar tasks, check aligned marker pairs and infer whether intervening cells should be filled, while preserving unrelated cells; validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: cautiously connect aligned marker intervals","content":"In some ARC tasks with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, aligned markers in a row or column are connected by recoloring the intervening background cells with a third color, while preserving markers and unrelated cells. Check intervals between consecutive markers on each line. Evidence: demonstrations with markers 6 or 5 used color 3 for intervals; a solved test with background 7 and markers 8 filled the intervening vertical cells with 3. This is a possible task rule, not a universal default—apply only when demonstrations support it.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves a reusable, evidence-backed task pattern while explicitly limiting overgeneralization.","after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: cautiously connect aligned marker intervals","content":"In some ARC tasks with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, aligned markers in a row or column are connected by recoloring the intervening background cells with a third color, while preserving markers and unrelated cells. Check intervals between consecutive markers on each line. Evidence: demonstrations with markers 6 or 5 used color 3 for intervals; a solved test with background 7 and markers 8 filled the intervening vertical cells with 3. This is a possible task rule, not a universal default—apply only when demonstrations support it.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114628304","summary":"Updated the global ARC memory with the demonstrated row-and-column connection rule.","rationale":"The demo and correct test submission validate filling the background between the outermost same-color markers on each shared row or column with the third color, while preserving markers and unrelated cells.","expectedOutcome":"Future ARC instances with this pattern should check both axes, combine the fills, and retain all original cells outside the intervening background intervals.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells between the outermost markers with the third color; preserve all original markers and unrelated cells. The result is the union of horizontal and vertical fills. Validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it. Demonstrated with markers of color 4 on background 1 joined using color 3, and a correct test submission with markers of color 8 on background 0 joined using color 3.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The trajectory provides a demonstration and a correctly solved test confirming this reusable rule and its preservation constraints.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: cautiously connect aligned marker intervals","content":"In some ARC tasks with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, aligned markers in a row or column are connected by recoloring the intervening background cells with a third color, while preserving markers and unrelated cells. Check intervals between consecutive markers on each line. Evidence: demonstrations with markers 6 or 5 used color 3 for intervals; a solved test with background 7 and markers 8 filled the intervening vertical cells with 3. This is a possible task rule, not a universal default—apply only when demonstrations support it.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells between the outermost markers with the third color; preserve all original markers and unrelated cells. The result is the union of horizontal and vertical fills. Validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it. Demonstrated with markers of color 4 on background 1 joined using color 3, and a correct test submission with markers of color 8 on background 0 joined using color 3.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:33.041Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114658956","summary":"Updated the global ARC memory with the confirmed marker-interval rule and test evidence.","rationale":"The demo shows aligned 9 markers connected through intervening cells using color 3; the solved test confirms the same transformation for 0 markers on background 2, while an unpaired marker stays unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future similar ARC tasks should fill only background cells strictly between aligned same-color endpoints, preserve endpoints and unrelated cells, and leave unpaired markers unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells strictly between the outermost aligned markers, preserving the marker endpoints and all other cells. Demonstrated recurrence: markers 9 on background 4 were connected with color 3 horizontally and vertically; markers 0 on background 2 had the intervening cells between a horizontal pair filled with 3, while an unpaired marker remained unchanged. Validate that this rule fits the task demonstrations before applying it.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a successful recurrence and specific evidence while retaining the cautious, interval-only rule.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells between the outermost markers with the third color; preserve all original markers and unrelated cells. The result is the union of horizontal and vertical fills. Validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it. Demonstrated with markers of color 4 on background 1 joined using color 3, and a correct test submission with markers of color 8 on background 0 joined using color 3.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:46:33.041Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells strictly between the outermost aligned markers, preserving the marker endpoints and all other cells. Demonstrated recurrence: markers 9 on background 4 were connected with color 3 horizontally and vertically; markers 0 on background 2 had the intervening cells between a horizontal pair filled with 3, while an unpaired marker remained unchanged. Validate that this rule fits the task demonstrations before applying it.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:04.634Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114735179","summary":"Updated the global ARC memory with confirmed evidence for filling aligned marker intervals on both axes.","rationale":"A demonstration confirmed that marker cells are connected through the background using a third color, and applying that rule to the test grid solved the instance. The requested rule also specifies using the original grid to identify intervals before combining fills.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching ARC tasks should identify consecutive same-color markers in each original row and column, fill only strictly intervening background cells with the demonstrated third color, and preserve markers and unrelated cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the original grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. For each pair, recolor only background cells strictly between the endpoints with the demonstrated third color; preserve marker cells and unrelated cells. Collect all row and column intervals from the original grid before combining fills, so fills created along one axis do not become markers for the other. A demo with marker 5 and background 6 confirmed third color 3; applying the same rule with marker 2 and background 7 solved task-592e9029 correctly.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds successful task evidence and clarifies consecutive-marker detection, fill preservation, and use of the original grid.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, check both rows and columns for two or more markers of that color. For each qualifying row or column, recolor only the background cells strictly between the outermost aligned markers, preserving the marker endpoints and all other cells. Demonstrated recurrence: markers 9 on background 4 were connected with color 3 horizontally and vertically; markers 0 on background 2 had the intervening cells between a horizontal pair filled with 3, while an unpaired marker remained unchanged. Validate that this rule fits the task demonstrations before applying it.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:04.634Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the original grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. For each pair, recolor only background cells strictly between the endpoints with the demonstrated third color; preserve marker cells and unrelated cells. Collect all row and column intervals from the original grid before combining fills, so fills created along one axis do not become markers for the other. A demo with marker 5 and background 6 confirmed third color 3; applying the same rule with marker 2 and background 7 solved task-592e9029 correctly.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:41.026Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114808080","summary":"Updated the global ARC memory with confirmed evidence for filling aligned marker intervals on both axes.","rationale":"The demonstration and correctly solved test support the existing rule: use the original grid to find consecutive same-color markers in rows and columns, fill only intervening background cells with the demonstrated third color, and preserve everything else.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching ARC tasks should apply the rule consistently on both axes without changing markers or unrelated cells; validate by checking the output against the demonstration pattern.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the unmodified input grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. Fill only background cells strictly between each consecutive pair with the demonstrated fill color, preserving marker cells and all other cells. Determine intervals from the original grid on both axes, then combine the fills; leave unpaired markers unchanged. Confirmed by a demonstration with markers 5, background 8, and fill color 3, and a correctly solved test with markers 6, background 0, and fill color 3.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Add successful test evidence and explicitly preserve the original-grid, consecutive-pair, and background-only constraints.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the original grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. For each pair, recolor only background cells strictly between the endpoints with the demonstrated third color; preserve marker cells and unrelated cells. Collect all row and column intervals from the original grid before combining fills, so fills created along one axis do not become markers for the other. A demo with marker 5 and background 6 confirmed third color 3; applying the same rule with marker 2 and background 7 solved task-592e9029 correctly.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:41.026Z","version":4},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the unmodified input grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. Fill only background cells strictly between each consecutive pair with the demonstrated fill color, preserving marker cells and all other cells. Determine intervals from the original grid on both axes, then combine the fills; leave unpaired markers unchanged. Confirmed by a demonstration with markers 5, background 8, and fill color 3, and a correctly solved test with markers 6, background 0, and fill color 3.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:13.700Z","version":5},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114846707","summary":"Updated the existing global aligned-marker memory with this confirmed row-and-column interval-fill evidence.","rationale":"The demo and correctly solved test confirm that consecutive matching markers are connected on both axes by filling only intervening background cells with 3, while preserving endpoints. This reinforces the existing task-family rule without extending it beyond that family.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching ARC tasks should check rows and columns using the original grid, preserve marker endpoints, and combine fills between consecutive matching markers; the demonstrated cases use fill color 3.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid. In every row and column, find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color and fill only the strictly intervening background cells, preserving markers and all unrelated cells. Combine horizontal and vertical fills. Demonstrations confirmed fill color 3 for background 6 with marker 9, and the same rule with background 9 and marker 1 was correctly applied. Validate the pattern against demonstrations; do not assume it applies outside this task family.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds confirmed evidence from a solved instance to the existing reusable memory while keeping the rule limited to its demonstrated task family.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform background and sparse same-color markers, inspect the unmodified input grid for consecutive occurrences of the marker color in every row and column. Fill only background cells strictly between each consecutive pair with the demonstrated fill color, preserving marker cells and all other cells. Determine intervals from the original grid on both axes, then combine the fills; leave unpaired markers unchanged. Confirmed by a demonstration with markers 5, background 8, and fill color 3, and a correctly solved test with markers 6, background 0, and fill color 3.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:13.700Z","version":5},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid. In every row and column, find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color and fill only the strictly intervening background cells, preserving markers and all unrelated cells. Combine horizontal and vertical fills. Demonstrations confirmed fill color 3 for background 6 with marker 9, and the same rule with background 9 and marker 1 was correctly applied. Validate the pattern against demonstrations; do not assume it applies outside this task family.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:52.709Z","version":6},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115608007","summary":"Updated the global ARC aligned-marker memory to reaffirm the demonstrated rule and add a grid-transcription verification safeguard.","rationale":"The same interval-fill rule eventually solved task-592e9029 after correcting a transcription error that shifted a zero and created false alignments; the rejected outputs do not justify changing the rule.","expectedOutcome":"For matching tasks, preserve the demonstrated fill behavior while checking parsed rows against the displayed input before deriving or submitting output; validate by confirming row widths and cell-by-cell transcription.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes (general, v7)","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid, identify the dominant uniform background and sparse marker color, and find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color in every row and column. Fill only the strictly intervening background cells with color 3; preserve marker endpoints and all unrelated cells. Apply horizontal and vertical fills using the original grid, then combine the fills. Critical safeguard: parse each displayed row from its space-separated cell tokens, or independently verify any compact digit-string transcription against every source row before solving. In task-592e9029, repeated rejected outputs came from a transcription error that shifted a zero from column 11 to column 10, inventing vertical intervals; correcting the transcription made this rule succeed. Do not revise the rule based on outputs derived from an unchecked transcription.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The solved instance confirms the existing rule and provides concrete evidence that transcription validation prevents false alignments and repeated incorrect submissions.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid. In every row and column, find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color and fill only the strictly intervening background cells, preserving markers and all unrelated cells. Combine horizontal and vertical fills. Demonstrations confirmed fill color 3 for background 6 with marker 9, and the same rule with background 9 and marker 1 was correctly applied. Validate the pattern against demonstrations; do not assume it applies outside this task family.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:52.709Z","version":6},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes (general, v7)","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid, identify the dominant uniform background and sparse marker color, and find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color in every row and column. Fill only the strictly intervening background cells with color 3; preserve marker endpoints and all unrelated cells. Apply horizontal and vertical fills using the original grid, then combine the fills. Critical safeguard: parse each displayed row from its space-separated cell tokens, or independently verify any compact digit-string transcription against every source row before solving. In task-592e9029, repeated rejected outputs came from a transcription error that shifted a zero from column 11 to column 10, inventing vertical intervals; correcting the transcription made this rule succeed. Do not revise the rule based on outputs derived from an unchecked transcription.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:13.824Z","version":7},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115619596","summary":"Updated the global aligned-marker memory with the confirmed rule and a transcription-validation safeguard.","rationale":"The corrected input and unchanged interval-fill rule solved task-592e9029; repeated failures came from a manually compressed row that shifted a zero and introduced false connections.","expectedOutcome":"For matching ARC tasks, preserve the demonstrated row-and-column fill behavior while validating every parsed row and any compact transcription against the displayed input before deriving or submitting an output.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid to identify the dominant uniform background and sparse marker color. In each original row and column, consider consecutive occurrences of the same marker color; recolor only intervening cells that are the background with color 3. Preserve marker endpoints and all unrelated cells, and combine horizontal and vertical fills. Validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it. Critical input safeguard: parse displayed space-separated cells directly when possible. If using compact digit-string rows, verify each token against the displayed source row, and audit row lengths and cell positions before solving or submitting. In task-592e9029, a manual transcription shifted a zero in row 12 from column 11 to column 10, creating false vertical intervals and repeated rejected outputs. Correcting the transcription while keeping the rule unchanged produced a correct answer.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This records the confirmed transformation and a broadly reusable, evidence-backed safeguard against transcription errors that caused repeated failures.","before":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes (general, v7)","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid, identify the dominant uniform background and sparse marker color, and find consecutive occurrences of the same marker color in every row and column. Fill only the strictly intervening background cells with color 3; preserve marker endpoints and all unrelated cells. Apply horizontal and vertical fills using the original grid, then combine the fills. Critical safeguard: parse each displayed row from its space-separated cell tokens, or independently verify any compact digit-string transcription against every source row before solving. In task-592e9029, repeated rejected outputs came from a transcription error that shifted a zero from column 11 to column 10, inventing vertical intervals; correcting the transcription made this rule succeed. Do not revise the rule based on outputs derived from an unchecked transcription.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:13.824Z","version":7},"after":{"id":"arc_cautiously_connect_aligned_marker_intervals","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: connect aligned marker intervals on both axes","content":"For ARC grids matching the demonstrated uniform-background, sparse-marker task family, inspect the original grid to identify the dominant uniform background and sparse marker color. In each original row and column, consider consecutive occurrences of the same marker color; recolor only intervening cells that are the background with color 3. Preserve marker endpoints and all unrelated cells, and combine horizontal and vertical fills. Validate the rule against demonstrations before applying it. Critical input safeguard: parse displayed space-separated cells directly when possible. If using compact digit-string rows, verify each token against the displayed source row, and audit row lengths and cell positions before solving or submitting. In task-592e9029, a manual transcription shifted a zero in row 12 from column 11 to column 10, creating false vertical intervals and repeated rejected outputs. Correcting the transcription while keeping the rule unchanged produced a correct answer.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:44:54.508Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:56:24.383Z","version":8},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115754977","summary":"Create a global ARC memory for completing matching repeated motifs by marking the corresponding missing or anomalous segment with color 1.","rationale":"Three demonstrations and the correctly solved test show color 1 marking the corresponding tail or cell in repeated motif rows or blocks; the task-specific rule is distinct from the existing aligned-marker memories.","expectedOutcome":"For similar ARC tasks, compare repeated motif rows or blocks, identify the corresponding segment indicated by the matching copy, and mark only that segment with 1 while preserving other cells; validate the alignment against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_complete_repeated_motif_segments_with_color_1","title":"ARC: mark corresponding repeated-motif segment with color 1","content":"For ARC grids where repeated rows or blocks contain a recognizable shared motif and corresponding segments differ, compare the copies to locate the indicated tail, missing region, or anomalous cell. Mark only the corresponding segment with color 1, preserving all other cells; do not blindly fill every background tail. Demonstrations showed color 1 extending motif rows at demo 1 rows 3–4, columns 8–9; demo 2 rows 3–6, columns 17–21; and demo 3 row 7, columns 8–13. In the solved test, the matching row indicated replacing the lone contrasting cell at row 0, column 13 with 1. Validate by checking the proposed segment against the aligned repeated motif.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Capture the demonstrated, reusable pattern-completion behavior and its alignment safeguard.","after":{"id":"arc_complete_repeated_motif_segments_with_color_1","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: mark corresponding repeated-motif segment with color 1","content":"For ARC grids where repeated rows or blocks contain a recognizable shared motif and corresponding segments differ, compare the copies to locate the indicated tail, missing region, or anomalous cell. Mark only the corresponding segment with color 1, preserving all other cells; do not blindly fill every background tail. Demonstrations showed color 1 extending motif rows at demo 1 rows 3–4, columns 8–9; demo 2 rows 3–6, columns 17–21; and demo 3 row 7, columns 8–13. In the solved test, the matching row indicated replacing the lone contrasting cell at row 0, column 13 with 1. Validate by checking the proposed segment against the aligned repeated motif.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:58:02.824Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:58:02.824Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/9c086a91621049f09b6809851224e395/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115838135","summary":"Updated the global repeated-motif memory with the validated rule for marking missing trailing motif segments with color 1.","rationale":"A correct submission confirmed that aligned repeated rows can indicate a missing suffix: preserve the shared motif, recolor only the corresponding background suffix to 1, and leave all other cells unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future matching ARC tasks should identify aligned repeated rows or blocks, compare corresponding segments, and mark only the missing trailing background cells with 1; validate that dimensions and unrelated cells are preserved.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_complete_repeated_motif_segments_with_color_1","title":"ARC: mark corresponding repeated-motif segment with color 1 (general, v2)","content":"For ARC grids with repeated aligned rows or blocks containing a recognizable shared motif, compare corresponding segments to find a missing or anomalous part. A confirmed variation is a missing trailing segment: when one copy has a suffix of the uniform background where the corresponding segment in the matching copy is motif-colored, recolor only that background suffix to 1. Demonstrated examples include rows 0 and 17 of a 20x30 grid, where the color-7 prefix is followed by background 4; the output changes only those suffix cells to 1. In a test with matching two-row patterns at rows 0–1 and 17–18, the lower copy was missing color 5 at columns 11–15, so only those background 0 cells became 1. Preserve shared motif cells, all other cells, and dimensions.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"This specific repeated-motif transformation was validated by a correct submission and clarifies which cells to change while preserving unrelated content.","before":{"id":"arc_complete_repeated_motif_segments_with_color_1","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: mark corresponding repeated-motif segment with color 1","content":"For ARC grids where repeated rows or