{"id":"refine_20260929130837998","summary":"Created a global ARC memory for restoring solid rectangular color patches obscured by isolated noise markers.","rationale":"The task was solved correctly after one demonstration established that solid rectangular patches should be restored to their base colors and isolated anomalies outside them cleared to the background.","expectedOutcome":"For matching ARC tasks, identify patch bounds and colors from intact portions and the demonstration, restore anomalous cells inside patches, and clear isolated noise outside; validate that unrelated background cells and grid dimensions remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_restore_rectangular_patches_and_remove_isolated_noise","title":"Restore rectangular color patches obscured by isolated noise","content":"For ARC grids with a uniform outer background and multiple solid rectangular color patches, scattered single-cell noise or marker colors may overwrite cells inside patches and appear outside them. Use intact portions and demonstration behavior to infer each rectangle's bounds and base color, then restore every cell within each identified patch to that color. Replace isolated noise outside patches with the outer background. Do not assume every non-background cell belongs to a patch: preserve unrelated background cells, including rectangles whose base color matches a distinct interior/background value, and infer patch boundaries cautiously from geometry and examples. Validate dimensions and ensure only identified patches and isolated anomalies are changed. This rule was validated on a task where restoring nine rectangles and clearing external markers produced the correct output.","metadata":{"scope":"global","domain":"ARC"},"reason":"A demonstration and successful test submission validated this reusable patch-restoration rule.","after":{"id":"arc_restore_rectangular_patches_and_remove_isolated_noise","kind":"memory","title":"Restore rectangula